        "calls": 1,
        "text": "The limit on how many times a billboard ad can appear to a single person is now set separately for the side panel and the main right panel, instead of using one flat number for both. This means the side panel will show the same advertiser at most three times a day (with at most one appearance in any given hour), while the main panel will show a specific ad only once a day. This prevents one advertiser from taking over the entire day's view by spreading out their ads more fairly. There is no action you need to take; the system handles these limits automatically.",
